==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l UFO Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Flying Cat''' when obtained from [[Tiny Wings (Deadly)|Li'l Bird Awakens!]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], Li'l Bird Cat suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, which makes it underperform greatly in its field. For this reason, usage of Li'l Bird Cat prior to unlocking its True Form is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
Although its health and range still leave it highly vulnerable, Li'l Flying Cat's anti-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] perks allow it to take a specialized role as one of the few spammable anti-Zombie damage-dealers. Li'l Flying Cat annihilates most Zombie peons, even [[Zory|Zories]], although it can't handle [[Zir Zeal]], [[Zang Roo]] and a few others due to lack of range. Despite this, it serves as a great Zombie Killer, just make sure you aren't overwhelmed when those dangerous enemies burrow under your front line.

To improve its performance, but also due to the lack of accessible alternatives for dealing with Zombies in {{4c}} stages, it is recommended to upgrade Li'l Flying Cat whenever possible, though once you obtain [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]], this unit cannot perform well compared to the aforementioned two.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Target Relic''' and '''Curse Immune''' give Li'l Flying rather decent stats against [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]], especially in {{4c}} stages or no-gacha strats. While he does outrange very few Relics, he really works well against those few. He can notably shine against a swarm of [[Sir Rel]] or even [[Primeval Cyclone]] with proper team support. Unfortunately, Li'l Flying Cat is outclassed by [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] and especially [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]], which require little to no investment and are much more efficient at the task.

Similarly, '''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' work really well, assuming that Li'l Flying is already boosted with [[Catseye]]s, to really improve his stats against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] and Relics.

'''Curse''', however, is not really useful. It can prevent Relics from themselves cursing your Cats, as situational as that can be, as well as potentially helping against a few Zombies. However, most Zombies are stat-based and thus not hindered by Curse for the most part. It is also outclassed by [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]], who can do so at a far greater range.

==='''Orb'''===
Cash Back and Cost Down could see use for reducing Li'l Bird's high cost in a similar way to [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]. Thus, a Strong Up Orb for Zombie or Relic is the best way to go.

